  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_32bc688425e0480da3e44e9f91ece1a8",
      "statement": "External alerts arrive on a single public webhook route where the integration id in the URL path is the only credential, so that identifier must be treated as a secret.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L71-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca143e7974463cf02b9fd0958bb033c20ae296896078ca7580032ff06561119f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L155-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28fee115be26462bef078ab21632cba571b93ae81c01844b63d4fd476bc89cfe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c9c227e7782845c8843f9fc266123138",
      "statement": "A webhook is rejected unless the integration exists, is active, and its stored type matches the type segment in the URL, which prevents one provider's payload from being posted to another provider's integration and silently misparsed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L71-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b7fe5a124a66ab49832c58a7e22ec6ff47f3a2e90a8e05a42bd44768b0c869a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6d6edcaeb2964ce0a15b7e1baf751112",
      "statement": "Updating the integration heartbeat is best-effort during webhook processing: a failure is logged and the alert is still processed, so health bookkeeping cannot cause an alert to be dropped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L105-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f4206a9c3e4f50608b3f32513ec271f6a6e70f9a7fca58cadd51c16f2f207d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_adaa1ee7410b46baa816b89c253e89d6",
      "statement": "Seven provider types — prometheus, datadog, grafana, pagerduty, coralogix, generic webhook and aws — are dispatched to dedicated processors, with any unrecognised type falling through to the generic processor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L112-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb4f73a61957f19b88d0062e803c6e582c68f131001f940cc4349869475f537b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b18d570f48524cfcb00d42aec4aaee15",
      "statement": "Every provider processor converts its payload into a common ProcessedAlert shape carrying alert name, description, summary, severity, priority, status, labels and fingerprint, so all downstream routing operates on one representation regardless of source.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L112-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb4f73a61957f19b88d0062e803c6e582c68f131001f940cc4349869475f537b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L166-L201",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc20fbe10cebd568ec8acaa4ea65b80139d863b4b2883d3136f91bb058399f81:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e04d34cc69b40988f007ff85f5c130e",
      "statement": "Provider statuses are normalized to the two values firing and resolved, and every status mapper defaults an unrecognised value to firing rather than resolved.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L1236-L1246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f9d2d19004e2fd19371200d484b700c226aaa7e7b3c8bf2df21e04b5d35ce8a:"
