    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2e63e51fc334140b277ede59df95d63",
      "statement": "Alerts are routed by normalized status — firing creates an incident, resolved resolves one, and an unknown status is logged and treated as firing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L676-L689",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69fcc63abfd15b14c8447471f7c4871f5a485ec3ab71d422fac4b0ff4a995c6c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_49f1de58e0e24b45acc6be43642a7132",
      "statement": "Each alert in a webhook batch is routed independently and a failure on one is logged while the loop continues, so a single malformed alert does not discard the rest of the batch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L144-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6891dd6f09090344dd74acdbf0a1c456a57da9444ec33b803f545800c2048c15:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28a553efb1114939b1bd0ae644bf4419",
      "statement": "A firing alert carrying a fingerprint is checked against existing incidents first, and on a match the existing incident's alert count is incremented instead of creating a duplicate, so a flapping alert produces one incident with a rising count.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L690-L706",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5a7763f6b637d68130421656df11d4714c7abfe43654acd9d66fa4e2639bed8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f12744076de4880815142d011d2bf58",
      "statement": "The alert fingerprint is written into the incident's labels at creation time, which is what makes the later fingerprint-based lookup on resolution possible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L1040-L1048",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce99f641058ae3707e4370109b1ff67d7bb1262916e197d8465eeb427de9789c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66ebfd01bd614b478ba9f88204ad9ab6",
      "statement": "Service and assignee resolution runs before incident creation so the incident is written once with all associations already attached, rather than being created and then updated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/webhook.go#L705-L723",
